Seymour\\n\\n- Anne of Cleves\\n\\n- Catherine Howard\\n\\n- Catherine Parr\\n\\nThe First Wife: Henry VIII and Catherine of Aragon\\n\\nName: Catherine of Aragon\\n\\nMarriage Dates: 1509–1533\\n\\nChildren: Henry, Duke of Cornwall; Mary I of England\\n\\nHenry ... \",\"title\":\"https://study.com/academy/lesson/henry-vii-the-kings-great-matter-and-the-succession-acts.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d150\"},\"ref\":\"d150\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1536 - 1537 (Died)\\n\\nSurviving Children: Edward VI\\n\\nIn May 1536, Henry married Jane Seymour. Unlike his previous wives, Jane never had a coronation and so was never crowned queen. In October 1537, Henry finally got his wish with Jane giving birth to the future King Edward VI. Sadly ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/royal-history/who-were-henry-viiis-wives\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d151\"},\"ref\":\"d151\",\"snippet\":\" ... While Catherine Parr outlived Henry and was widowed when he died during their marriage, long-since annulled Anne of Cleves also survived him and was the last of his wives to die.\\n\\nDescendants and relationships\\n\\nCatherine of Aragon, Anne Boleyn, and Jane Seymour each gave Henry VIII one ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wives_of_Henry_VIII\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d152\"},\"ref\":\"d152\",\"snippet\":\" ... Pride and Prejudice, Jane Austen\\n\\nSometimes one is in the mood for a simple novel of manners and marriage, and obviously P&P is the example par excellence of that genre. — Michelle Dean\\n\\n15. David Copperfield, Charles Dickens\\n\\nDickens loved the faux-autobiography Copperfield the